<div class="test-card-title">20-Yard Shuttle</div>
<div class="test-card-sub">Short-area quickness &amp; lateral speed</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="test-what">
<strong>What it measures:</strong> Short-area quickness and lateral agility. Starting from the middle, the athlete runs 5 yards to one side, touches the line, sprints 10 yards to the opposite side, touches that line, then sprints back 5 yards to finish. It measures first-step quickness, lateral speed, and the ability to change direction under full speed — critical for defensive backs, linebackers, and receivers running underneath routes.
      </div>
